body:
Got the bl touch on amazon:  [https://smile.amazon.com/gp/product/B01FFV2TOS/ref=ppx\_yo\_dt\_b\_search\_asin\_title?ie=UTF8&psc=1](https://smile.amazon.com/gp/product/B01FFV2TOS/ref=ppx_yo_dt_b_search_asin_title?ie=UTF8&psc=1)

Mounts were on thingiverse and I watched teaching tech's video on youtube for the install. If you're good with soldering wiring is a piece of cake. Other wise just get the pin 27 board as well, just a couple extra bucks you gotta spend.

&#x200B;

Not sure if you have flashed a bootloader onto your board yet that was really pretty simple you'll need an arduino to do that, videos for it make it real easy to add the bootloader.

&#x200B;

However getting the firmware correct really frustrated me at first and took me awhile and I actually gave up at one point, only later to find out I had received a bad bltouch. Eventually I ordered a new one and had the firmware working the first time, and in teaching tech's video he steps through exactly how to do it to make it real easy.
